TITLE:Who Saw What Spec
H1:P2 · Who saw what? (Day 15, a word from Tomas) <span class="draft">spec for approval</span>
SUB:The crew noticed the fault; you didn't. Ask the people who were there when it happened, and when. One of them may be honestly mixed up. A small new thing on Day 15, on the case engine, seat H. Plan Part 4, P2.
NAV:plain=In plain words|first=Your first P2|rules=How witnesses work|grow=How it grows|b=Builder|tests=Tests|faq=FAQ

<section id="plain">
  <h2>In plain words</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>A new button on a person's chat card: <b>Ask about the fault</b>. They say where they were, when, and what they noticed ("It rattled when I went to bed, about 22:00").</li>
    <li>What people noticed at a time crosses out the causes that couldn't show then. <b>Nobody lies</b>, but someone may be mixed up: their schedule (the Roster) had them somewhere else, so they mean a different machine. Spotting that is part of it.</li>
    <li>The Chief's notes, new page: "Ask who was there, and check they were."</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section id="first">
  <h2>Your first P2 (Day 15, Monday)</h2>
  <p>Tomas, at breakfast (he's off on Mondays): "You're asking around about the scrubber? Ask who sleeps near it. And check they were in." The case: <b>"Scrubber 2 on Deck 4 rattles now and then."</b> Suspects: the <b>filter</b> (clogged: rattles all the time), the <b>fan bearing</b> (rattles once it's run for hours: evenings), a <b>loose housing panel</b> (rattles when the door by it slams).</p>
  <div class="tablewrap"><table>
    <tr><th>Who (ask anywhere)</th><th>What they say</th><th>Crosses out</th></tr>
    <tr><td>Pell</td><td>"Quiet as anything at breakfast."</td><td>the filter (it would rattle all day)</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Rina</td><td>"Rattling at 19:30 while I sat in the common room. Nobody came or went; the door never moved."</td><td>the loose panel (it needs the door)</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Kovac</td><td>"It rattled at 13:00!" Her schedule had her on Deck 5 then: she means Deck 5's scrubber. An honest mix-up.</td><td>nothing (once you see the mix-up)</td></tr>
  </table></div>
  <p><b>It's the fan bearing.</b> Two witnesses, each crossing out one suspect; neither settles it alone. Fix: a Tier 2 repair, a bearing from the Galley parts shelf. The names are examples: the real witnesses are whoever was really there.</p>
</section>

<section id="rules">
  <h2>How witnesses work</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><b>Who knows:</b> crew whose real plan had them near the machine (same room or the next) during the fault's window; they're found by Roster as now.</li>
    <li><b>What they say:</b> at the time they were there, the machine was showing or not (from the cause's <code>when</code>); "showing at t" crosses out causes that can't show at t; "quiet at t" crosses out causes that would show at t.</li>
    <li><b>A mix-up</b> is a person whose plan had them elsewhere; their line is about the machine where they really were. It crosses out nothing, and the case must be solvable without it.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section id="grow">
  <h2>How it grows (bands)</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><b>T2</b>: 3-4 suspects, 2-3 witnesses plus at most one mix-up, one deck.</li>
    <li><b>T2+</b>: a witness on another shift (find them on the Roster, maybe at night), witnesses on two decks.</li>
    <li><b>T3</b>: two stories both true, pointing to two faults.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section id="b" class="builder">
  <h2>For the builder (seat H, the P2 kind in 24k)</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><code>CASE_KINDS.p2 = { ladder: 'p2', fits: causes differing in <code>when</code>, suspects: cause + decoys, clues: one <code>person</code> clue per chosen witness: { who, at, saw: true|false, kills } }</code>.</li>
    <li><b>Witnesses from the sim:</b> <code>planWhere(p, t)</code> over the fault's window (the 24 hours before posting); candidates are crew whose place was in the machine's room or an adjoining room; their minute is the middle of their stay; what they saw is the cause's real <code>when</code> at that minute. A mix-up is picked from crew on the Roster whose plan had them elsewhere (the same kind of machine on another deck), at most one per case, never needed.</li>
    <li><b>The Ask button</b> on the chat card (<code>chatOpen</code>, section 20): one line, typeof-guarded, shown only while a P2 case is open and the person is a witness or a mix-up; the answer is their line from <code>content/cases/p2.lines</code>; collecting it is <code>caseClue</code>.</li>
    <li><b>The ladder:</b> row <code>p2</code> (Day 15, small, Officer, <code>by: ['tomas', 'torres-zeke']</code>; it's a word, not a lesson, so an off-duty teacher counts if they're aboard and awake). First case: <code>4-scrubber-2</code>, cause <code>bearing</code> (when: warm), suspects filter (always), bearing, panel (touched; a new Tier 2 cause for the scrubber's table, part <code>seal</code>, sign "the housing buzzes when the door goes"); if <code>4-scrubber-2</code> is busy, <code>4-scrubber-1</code>.</li>
    <li><b>Keys:</b> 893 (witness choice), 894 (the mix-up).</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section id="tests" class="builder">
  <h2>Tests</h2>
  <ul><li><b><code>puzzle_check</code></b> (P2): every witness really was there at their minute (<code>planWhere</code>); every mix-up really was elsewhere; the case solves without the mix-up; no single witness solves it; the same twice.</li></ul>
</section>

<section id="faq">
  <h2>Builders' questions</h2>
  <p class="note">None yet.</p>
</section>
